  "summary": "Sarthebari Bell Metal Craft is a traditional metalcraft practiced in Sarthebari, a town in the Bajali district of Assam, India.",
  "description": "Sarthebari Bell Metal Craft is a traditional metalcraft practiced in Sarthebari, a town in the Bajali district of Assam, India. It is one of the most prominent handicraft traditions of the state and is widely known for its bell metal utensils, ritual objects, and musical instruments. The craft has played an important role in the cultural life of Assam and continues to provide livelihoods to a large number of artisan families.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Assam; registration 2023–24), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
